    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** anchors the Zurich Zebras lineup as our most valuable asset, boasting an elite score of 80.98. His combination of a favorable matchup against Chandler (xERA 4.71) and his premium speed profile makes him the cornerstone of our SB-focused strategy. Alongside him, **Trea Turner** (75.36) and **Yordan Alvarez** (70.49) provide the necessary high-floor production. **Trea Turner** leverages an advantageous spot in the two-hole against Holmes, while **Yordan Alvarez** maintains an elite 0.443 xwOBA despite the task of facing Peralta. **Colt Keith** and **Junior Caminero** also stand out as strong plays, both exceeding the 67-point mark by capitalizing on manageable matchups against Hughes and Wesneski, respectively.\n\nThe most challenging decision today was the exclusion of **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** from the active roster. While his score of 40.50 was technically marginal, he was squeezed out by the high efficiency of our platoon-advantaged outfielders. The optimizer prioritized the dynamic platoon edge afforded to **Lars Nootbaar** and **Christian Yelich**, leaving **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** on the bench to preserve our game caps. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Carson Benge**; while he is in the lineup, his score of 46.11 is dampened by a high-skill matchup against Schlittler (xERA 2.88). Though he maintains a platoon edge, the SP skill penalty is significant enough that we are monitoring his performance closely against a tough arm. With **Casey Schmitt**, **Josh Smith**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** unavailable due to injury or rest, our depth is tested, but the projected output from **Kazuma Okamoto** at UTIL should stabilize the middle of our order.",
